							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I&#039;ve never said EQ was dying, and in fact have said it&#039;s going to most likely be around for a long time to come. <br /><br />But the vast majority of what was FoT is now playing other games, no matter how you cut it. It actually started when EQ2, and WoW started thier beta phases, and just got worse as time went by.<br /><br />It was very obvious that the quality of players was going south, for christ sakes, Ascent took that one cleric, Nerika I think her name was, that we booted simply because she was so inept at playing the game as an app. That just shows that the skill level in general for content was not sustainable.<br /><br />With the guilds that have left the game in one way or another, it opened up the players to join to the other guilds that needed players. It&#039;s a simple shrinking of the player base, and it did not happen over night. It started with PoP, when the casual folks started leaving the game because unless you were in a raiding guild, you got shafted. LDoN brought some people back, but it never really recovered from what PoP did to the game.<br /><br />I really hate what has happened Bobo, EQ was fun for a long long time. In some respects, there are good things happening, and beleive it or not, if they would simply change a few more things, I honestly think EQ could still give WoW a real run for thier money.<br /><br />But the long term thing will be EQ2 vs WoW, with EQ mainly keeping the long term players at this rate.
