							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							There was a community and sense of purpose around EQ that i think any game out there currently is lacking.&nbsp; EQ was a game where you had a large group of people that for the most part all knew each other.&nbsp; <br /><br />Right now, playing WoW is a little like Diablo2 in the personality department, no one is really worried about their rep among other players on the server.&nbsp; They dont care if they KS, Camp steal, Hack, Dupe, Cheat, or swindle.&nbsp; I know a lot of them are young adults that were just looking for the Next Thing, and dont know how seriously some of us take a MMORPG.&nbsp; <br /><br />There are times that I miss EQ and the cool people that i have met and spent hours with there.&nbsp; Those times grow more frequent with each server crash, 90 second IF lag, and roll back.&nbsp; <br /><br />As for EQ server merges, it makes sense.&nbsp; Why pay more overhead then needed to publish a product to a smaller player base.&nbsp; &nbsp;I wish them luck.
